on settings\nL136:   * cite70†Fork3 (3) L137:   * cite70†Star36 (36) You must be signed in to star a repository\nL138: ## About\nL139: \nL140: PTXBench: an open-source environment for kernel agents with architecture-specifc CUDA/PTX\nL141: \nL142: ### Resources\nL143: \nL144: cite71†Readme L145: \nL146: cite72†Apache-2.0 license L147: \nL148: cite73†Activity L149: \nL150: ### Stars\nL151: \nL152: 36 stars\nL153: \nL154: ### Watchers\nL155: \nL156: 1 watching\nL157: \nL158: ### Forks\nL159: \nL160: cite74†3 forks L161: \nL162: cite75†Report repository L163: \nL164: main\nL165: \nL166: cite76†Branches cite77†Tags L167: \nL168: [Input: Go to file]\nL169: \nL170: Go to file\nL171: \nL172: Code\nL173: \nL174: Open more actions menu\nL175: \nL176: ## Latest commit\nL177: \nL178: \nL179: \nL180: ## History\nL181: \nL182: 67 Commits\nL183: ## Folders and files\nL184: Name  | Name  | Last commit message  | Last commit date\nL185: --- | --- | --- | ---\nL186: cite78†data | cite78†data |    |\nL187: cite79†experiments | cite79†experiments |    |\nL188: cite80†fib-profile | cite80†fib-profile |    |\nL189: cite81†img | cite81†img |    |\nL190: cite82†multiturn | cite82†multiturn |    |\nL191: cite83†ptxbench-eval | cite83†ptxbench-eval |    |\nL192: cite84†scripts | cite84†scripts |    |\nL193: cite85†.dockerignore | cite85†.dockerignore |    |\nL194: cite86†.env.example | cite86†.env.example |    |\nL195: cite87†.gitignore | cite87†.gitignore |    |\nL196: cite88†LICENSE | cite88†LICENSE |    |\nL197: cite89†NOTICE | cite89†NOTICE |    |\nL198: cite90†README.md | cite90†README.md |    |\nL199: cite91†pyproject.toml | cite91†pyproject.toml |    |\nL200: [Button: View all files]\nL201: ## Repository files navigation\nL202: \nL203:   *   * cite92†README L204:   * cite92†Apache-2.0 license L205: \nL206: More items\nL207: # PTXBench\nL208: \nL209: PTXBench contains one GPU profiling service and two ways to run kernel agents: the multiturn model loop and the coding-agent gateway. Fixit SFT and KernelGen use the same multiturn runner and prompt registry for source and final evaluation. This repository gives the experiment process and a small set of runnable examples; it does not include paper outputs, plots, or the full prepared experiment matrix.\nL210: Directory  | Purpose\nL211: --- | ---\nL212: `fib-profile/`  | GPU profiling service\nL213: `multiturn/`  | Model loop, CUDA/Triton evaluator tests, prompt registry, and runner\nL214: `ptxbench-eval/`  | Coding-agent gateway, launcher, agent images, and examples\nL215: `experiments/prepared/configs/`  | One multiturn config example\nL216: `experiments/fixit/`  | Failed-kernel repair, reasoning, SFT, serving, evaluation\nL217: `experiments/kernelgen/`  | Correct-kernel reasoning, SFT, serving, evaluation\nL218: `experiments/shared/`  | Run manifests, turn export, and shared training/serving code\nL219: 🚧 This repository is still under construction.\nL220: ## Setup\nL221: \nL222: Use Python 3.12, Docker with NVIDIA GPU access, `tmux`, and an H100 host for the bundled workloads. SFT runtime-SASS export also needs host `nvcc`, `cuobjdump`, and TVM-FFI headers/libraries. The profiling service has its own environment in the Docker image; install the host runner and coding-agent launcher separately:\nL223: \nL224:     python3.12 -m venv .venv\nL225:     source .venv/bin/activate\nL226:     pip install -e '.[sft,dev]'\nL227:     pip install -e ./ptxbench-eval\nL228:     pip install -r multiturn/requirements.txt\nL229: The SFT extra installs Tinker Cookbook for training and checkpoint handling. Training also needs a Tinker account. For evaluation alone, `pip install -e .` and the multiturn requirements suffice. Model provider credentials are read from environment variables; see `.env.example`.\nL230: Start the service using cite93†fib-profile/scripts/README.md . For the backward attention workloads, generate the two checksum-verified input blobs as described in cite94†fib-profile/dataset/README.md before starting the service. Check service health with:\nL231: \nL232:     curl -fsS http://localhost:10000/health\nL233: \nL234: Build the multiturn evaluator image:\nL235: \nL236:     docker build -f multiturn/docker/Dockerfile.eval -t ptxbench-multiturn-eval:latest .\nL237: ## Multiturn model loop\nL238: The runner expands a JSON config into trajectories and writes a `plan.json`, trajectories, logs, and success artifacts into a new output root. The shared prompt registry is `multiturn/prompts/hub.json`; assembled documents are under `multiturn/prompts/assembled`. The same runner supports CUDA and Triton test scripts under `multiturn/tests/`.\nL239: \nL240:     export GEMINI_API_KEY=...  # for this example model\nL241:     python multiturn/scripts/render.py --check\nL242:     python multiturn/run_parallel_v2.py \\\nL243:       --config experiments/prepared/configs/example.json \\\nL244:       --definition gemm_n7168_k5120 \\\nL245:       --test-path multiturn/tests/cuda/gemm_n7168_k5120.py \\\nL246:       --model gemini-3.1-pro-preview \\\nL247:       --service-url http://localhost:10000 \\\nL248:       --gpu-arch hopper --without-local-gpu \\\nL249:       --max-parallel 1 --max-profiles 1 \\\nL250:       --image ptxbench-multiturn-eval:latest \\\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nCAKE from Scratch: Agents Write GPU Kernels, and the Compiler Learns from Their Mistakes | Gang Liao (https://gangliao.me/blog/2026/cake-deep-dive/)\nciteturn35view3 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: yesterday; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://gangliao.me/blog/2026/cake-deep-dive/\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 718\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\ncannbot-skills/CHANGELOG.md-代码预览-cannbot-skills:基于 CANN 生态的 Agent 技能模块项目 - AtomGit (https://gitcode.com/cann/cannbot-skills/blob/master/CHANGELOG.md)\nciteturn35view4 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://gitcode.com/cann/cannbot-skills/blob/master/CHANGELOG.md\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 880\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n (https://raw.githubusercontent.com/AMD-AGI/GEAK/main/README.md)\nciteturn35view5 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: yesterday; Content type: text/plain; Source: find({\"ref_id\":\"turn33view0\",\"pattern\":\"Release\"}); Total lines: 253\nNo matching text found for \"Release\"--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n (https://raw.githubusercontent.com/alibaba/atrex-kernel-agent/v0.3.0/README.md)\nciteturn35view6 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 3 days ago; Content type: text/plain; Source: find({\"ref_id\":\"turn33view1\",\"pattern\":\"September\"}); Total lines: 117\nNo matching text found for \"September\""
